From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 19:13:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 117/119] optslp: loads move before a loop only when nothing
 can tell

Invariant-load hoisting took the parameters of include, exclude and other
inline routines that write them for reads, so the loop updated the hoisted
copy and the store was lost. It also hoisted loads out of loops that a goto
can enter, and before a statement of the first iteration that raises an
exception (an integer division by zero then raised EAccessViolation
instead). Loops with a label are now left alone, the parameters of inline
routines other than those known to only read them count as stores, and a
load moves only when the first iteration dereferences its pointer before
anything that can raise or store where an exception handler sees it; later
loads through that pointer read the same object. tests/test/opt/tslp3.pp;
tslp2's negated condition now uses a boolean, which keeps lnf_checknegate.
---
